From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 19:44:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(open-items): let codex-native run the open items tools
 without a prompt

In Codex's default "Ask for approval" mode, every call to
sys_open_items_raise, sys_open_items_update and sys_open_items_list stopped
the turn at an MCP elicitation ("Allow the omnigent MCP server to run tool
...?"). The instruction asks the agent to raise every question as an item,
so a session that plans anything stalled on prompts for its own
bookkeeping.

Add the three names to the tools codex-native pre-approves, the same
per-tool `approval_mode = "approve"` tables `sys_session_rename` already
gets. Pre-approval is safe because the tools read and write only the
calling session's own open items list: the server accepts raises and agent
updates only from that session's bound runner, and nothing else in the
session or on the host changes. Every other MCP tool keeps the session's
approval mode.

Not proposed upstream yet; it goes with the open items tools.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
